<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 24.38 at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 24.38 at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	24.38	    +  5	    24.00     24.49</p>
<p>91-Day	28.07	    + 48	    25.71     28.37</p>
<p>182-Day     30.41	    + 14	    27.90     30.49</p>
<p>336-Day     30.94				30.73     31.24</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 31.00 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.108 bln pesos    3.45</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.349 bln pesos    3.72</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   2.953 bln pesos    3.28</p>
<p>336-Day     600 million pesos   2.287 bln pesos    3.81</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.54 on demand of 11.70 billion pesos compared with 3.39 the week before on demand of 11.18 billion pesos.  </p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   11  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    3  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   8  basis points</p>
<p>    336-Day			   3 basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559. e-mail at robert.kozak@reuters.com</p>
</text>
